Lineweights, text heights, dimensions and hatches follow different rules between model and plot, and people who draw every day find them hard to remember. Measured in CADCraft (drawing in mm, A3 layout, viewport at 1:100 and 1:50, PDFs measured):
- a line with lineweight 0.50 mm comes out 0.50 mm at any scale, and on screen it doesn't show until lineweights are turned on (LWDISPLAY starts at 0);
- a text 250 high comes out 2.5 mm at 1:100 and 5 mm at 1:50;
- a dimension with DIMSCALE 1 at 1:100 comes out with 0.025 mm text, that is invisible;
- the same dashed line comes out dashed in the layout and continuous when plotting the model at 1:100 (it needs LTSCALE 100; MSLTSCALE doesn't exist).

An idea, **only in the layout (inside a viewport) and in the Plot dialog**:
- in the Properties palette an "On paper" row, for example "plots 0.35 mm (from the CTB: colour 3 → 0.35)", "text 2.5 mm high at 1:100", "dimension: 0.025 mm text, too small";
- a "how it plots" preview, true to lineweights and CTB, that can be turned on in the layout.

In the model no panel and no warnings: at most the preview on request.

